import tests/games/snake/motion.dl

set game to a new snake session
begin a run in the address of game
store a snake cell at 4 and 5 into game's body at 0
store a snake cell at 4 and 4 into game's body at 1
set game's direction to 2
set game's progress to 0.6
set position to the snake position 0 in (the address of game)
require condition ((the absolute value of (position's column - 4.0)) < 0.000001) reporting "The head left its column before turning"
require condition ((the absolute value of (position's row - 5.6)) < 0.000001) reporting "The head was drawn behind its current movement"
turn the address of game toward 1
set position to the snake position 0 in (the address of game)
require condition ((the absolute value of (position's column - 4.6)) < 0.000001) reporting "The turn did not redirect the current fractional move"
require condition ((the absolute value of (position's row - 5.0)) < 0.000001) reporting "Turning retained the abandoned vertical move"
require condition ((game's steps = 0) and (game's progress = 0.6)) reporting "Turning committed a tick or reset its progress"
turn the address of game toward 2
require condition (game's direction = 2) reporting "A second valid turn during the same tick was discarded"
turn the address of game toward 0
require condition (game's direction = 2) reporting "A turn back into the neck was allowed"

# A pending move toward the right wall can still be redirected before its tick.
begin a run in the address of game
store a snake cell at 23 and 5 into game's body at 0
store a snake cell at 22 and 5 into game's body at 1
set game's direction to 1
set game's progress to 0.6
turn the address of game toward 0
update the address of game after 0.05 seconds
require condition (game's phase = the playing screen) reporting "An abandoned move hit the wall"
require condition ((the item at 0 in (game's body)) is the same cell as (a snake cell at 23 and 4)) reporting "The redirected move did not commit its new destination"

# Contact ends the game at the next tick, then the already-failed run animates.
begin a run in the address of game
store a snake cell at 23 and 5 into game's body at 0
store a snake cell at 22 and 5 into game's body at 1
store a snake cell at 21 and 5 into game's body at 2
store a snake cell at 20 and 5 into game's body at 3
store a snake cell at 19 and 5 into game's body at 4
set game's direction to 1
update the address of game after 0.119 seconds
require condition (game's phase = the playing screen) reporting "A future wall collision ended the game early"
set position to the snake position 0 in (the address of game)
require condition (position's column < 24.0) reporting "The head crossed the wall before contact"
update the address of game after 0.002 seconds
require condition ((game's phase = the finished screen) and game's impact) reporting "The collision tick did not end the game and begin its impact animation"
set {impact steps} to game's steps
turn the address of game toward 0
require condition (game's direction = 1) reporting "Input changed a run after the collision tick"
update the address of game after 0.14 seconds
set head to the snake position 0 in (the address of game)
set neck to the snake position 1 in (the address of game)
require condition ((head's column - neck's column) < 0.9) reporting "The body did not compress behind the head"
require condition ((head's column <= 24.0) and (head's column > 23.5)) reporting "The impact animation crossed the wall or recoiled too far"
require condition (game's steps = impact steps) reporting "The game kept simulating during the impact animation"
update the address of game after 0.25 seconds
update the address of game after 0.25 seconds
require condition (game's impact time = the snake impact duration) reporting "The impact animation did not settle"
require condition (game's phase = the finished screen) reporting "The impact animation restarted the game"
begin a run in the address of game
require condition ((game's impact = false) and (game's progress = 0.0)) reporting "Restart retained motion or impact state"

# Wrapping crosses the seam without forecasting a wall collision.
set game's wrap edges to true
store a snake cell at 23 and 5 into game's body at 0
store a snake cell at 22 and 5 into game's body at 1
set game's progress to 0.6
set position to the snake position 0 in (the address of game)
require condition ((the absolute value of (position's column - 23.6)) < 0.000001) reporting "Wrapping advanced the visible head before it reached the seam"
update the address of game after 0.05 seconds
require condition ((game's phase = the playing screen) and ((the item at 0 in (game's body))'s column = 0)) reporting "Wrapping failed at the next tick"
turn the address of game toward 3
require condition (game's direction = 1) reporting "A turn back into the neck across the wrapped seam was allowed"
close the address of game

# Splitting a frame preserves the same simulation and fractional position.
set game to a new snake session
set peer to a new snake session
begin a run in the address of game
begin a run in the address of peer
set game's food to a snake cell at 0 and 0
set peer's food to a snake cell at 0 and 0
update the address of game after 0.25 seconds
update the address of peer after 0.1 seconds
update the address of peer after 0.15 seconds
set first to the snake position 0 in (the address of game)
set second to the snake position 0 in (the address of peer)
require condition ((game's steps = peer's steps) and ((the absolute value of (first's column - second's column)) < 0.000001)) reporting "Frame splitting changed the snake's actual position"
pause or resume the address of game
set game's pace to 0
update the address of game after 0.25 seconds
set position to the snake position 0 in (the address of game)
require condition ((position's column = first's column) and (position's row = first's row)) reporting "Changing pace or waiting while paused moved the snake"
close the address of game
close the address of peer
print "Snake motion passed" as a line
